      "writtenOn": "2018-03-19T09:20:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a concurrent access problem too: the host command might asynchronously modify it too.\nA well-behaved host is NOT supposed to do so, as it is waiting for the event triggered by its command to happen before doing something else.\nbut for random mis-behaving host, this is limiting a few weird effects when I\u0027m evaluating several time sensor_mode below.\nUsing a big fat mutex would only mildly help overall, either we lock just around a specific operation (but this is still assuming the host is well behaving wrt its sequence of operations) or we keep it for the full operation (but the host command would timeout which is not so great)",
      "parentUuid": "9c1009a6_ee5c840e",
